# Always-human paths. Code-owner review is required here whatever the risk tier says
# (enable "Require review from Code Owners" in branch protection or the ruleset).
# The last matching pattern wins. There is no `*` catch-all on purpose: with code-owner review required it
# would put a person on every PR and cancel the no-human tier. Paths not listed get their approvals from
# the tier check (classify.py's humans_required as a required check).

/.github/                   @your-org/platform
/infra/                     @your-org/platform
/CODEOWNERS                 @your-org/platform
/docs/CODEOWNERS            @your-org/platform
/evals/                     @your-org/tech-leads
# Sensitive directories at any depth (no leading slash), matching the ** globs in risk-tiers.json.
auth/                       @your-org/security
billing/                    @your-org/payments @your-org/security
migrations/                 @your-org/data
installer/                  @your-org/release
# Agent configuration, reviewer instructions and the tier rules, at any depth (no leading slash), so nested
# workstreams count too. A PR must not change the agent's tools or lower its own tier without an owner.
# Covers Claude Code, Codex, Copilot and Gemini CLI; /.github/ above covers Copilot's copilot-instructions.md,
# instructions/, agents/, hooks/ and skills/. Drop the lines for assistants you do not use, and add any
# instruction file names you configure (Codex project_doc_fallback_filenames, Gemini context.fileName).
REVIEW.md                   @your-org/tech-leads
AGENTS.md                   @your-org/tech-leads
AGENTS.override.md          @your-org/tech-leads
CLAUDE.md                   @your-org/tech-leads
CLAUDE.local.md             @your-org/tech-leads
GEMINI.md                   @your-org/tech-leads
.claude/                    @your-org/tech-leads
.codex/                     @your-org/tech-leads
.gemini/                    @your-org/tech-leads
.agents/                    @your-org/tech-leads
.mcp.json                   @your-org/tech-leads
risk-tiers.json             @your-org/tech-leads
classify.py                 @your-org/tech-leads
